\text{Distance} = \sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}
\] Here, the points are \((2, 2)\) and \((-1, -1)\). So, we can substitute \(x_1 = 2\), \(y_1 = 2\), \(x_2 = -1\), and \(y_2 = -1\) into the formula. \[
\text{Distance} = \sqrt{((-1) - 2)^2 + ((-1) - 2)^2} = \sqrt{(-3)^2 + (-3)^2} = \sqrt{9 + 9} = \sqrt{18} = \sqrt{9 \cdot 2} = 3\sqrt{2}
\] </think> <answer> \(3\sqrt{2}\) </answer>

